WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.157 --> 00:00:01.356
- Good morning believe nation,

00:00:01.356 --> 00:00:05.675
today's message is turn
your no's into how can I's?

00:00:05.675 --> 00:00:07.789
Over to you Lori Grenier.

00:00:07.789 --> 00:00:10.151
(rooster crowing)

00:00:10.151 --> 00:00:12.763
♫ I wake up every mornin'

00:00:12.763 --> 00:00:15.469
♫ Espresso keep me goin'

00:00:15.469 --> 00:00:19.369
♫ I wake up every mornin'

00:00:19.369 --> 00:00:21.971
- To me, an entrepreneur is somebody who

00:00:21.971 --> 00:00:23.329
will do whatever it takes.

00:00:23.329 --> 00:00:24.162
- [Female Interviewer] Right.

00:00:24.162 --> 00:00:28.329
- They're driven, they are
"A-type" personalities,

00:00:30.299 --> 00:00:31.646
it's like they don't know the word no.

00:00:31.646 --> 00:00:33.204
And that's always been my mantra,

00:00:33.204 --> 00:00:35.057
I know no no's, just how can I?

00:00:35.057 --> 00:00:37.140
So when I see that person

00:00:38.179 --> 00:00:39.682
I know that no matter what,

00:00:39.682 --> 00:00:41.391
even if they have to pivot,

00:00:41.391 --> 00:00:42.849
you know, which is something that happens,

00:00:42.849 --> 00:00:44.188
maybe this isn't the best idea

00:00:44.188 --> 00:00:46.687
but something else is and
you're going to change it,

00:00:46.687 --> 00:00:48.130
they're still going to make it

00:00:48.130 --> 00:00:49.869
because they have what it takes

00:00:49.869 --> 00:00:52.017
to be a successful entrepreneur.

00:00:52.017 --> 00:00:53.067
- So I don't necessarily agree

00:00:53.067 --> 00:00:55.823
that every entrepreneur needs
to be a type A personality

00:00:55.823 --> 00:00:57.630
but you do need to be resourceful.

00:00:57.630 --> 00:00:59.915
I think it's one of the
most consistent things

00:00:59.915 --> 00:01:00.984
about entrepreneurship,

00:01:00.984 --> 00:01:03.902
is you have to learn to be resourceful.

00:01:03.902 --> 00:01:06.248
You're going to get a
lot of no's, expect it.

00:01:06.248 --> 00:01:09.548
There's this great clip
of Sylvester Stallone,

00:01:09.548 --> 00:01:12.663
where he says that he loves the word no,

00:01:12.663 --> 00:01:15.023
because it means yes.

00:01:15.023 --> 00:01:16.253
(laughing)

00:01:16.253 --> 00:01:19.753
- Challenge, I really just I just love it.

00:01:21.390 --> 00:01:23.549
You know, I love being told no.

00:01:23.549 --> 00:01:25.049
It just means yes.

00:01:25.981 --> 00:01:27.688
- I lot of people are afraid of no's,

00:01:27.688 --> 00:01:29.084
a lot of people are afraid of rejection

00:01:29.084 --> 00:01:32.502
and for that reason, a lot
of people have great ideas

00:01:32.502 --> 00:01:33.527
can do amazing things,

00:01:33.527 --> 00:01:35.830
you've got this genius thing inside you

00:01:35.830 --> 00:01:37.227
that never gets out there

00:01:37.227 --> 00:01:39.492
because you got one no.

00:01:39.492 --> 00:01:41.302
A lot of people turn
into the person who then

00:01:41.302 --> 00:01:42.860
because they got their one no

00:01:42.860 --> 00:01:44.242
and they never took that bet on themselves

00:01:44.242 --> 00:01:46.969
and they had to pull everyone
else down around them.

00:01:46.969 --> 00:01:49.561
And so what I want you
to do is fast forward

00:01:49.561 --> 00:01:51.538
to the end of your life,

00:01:51.538 --> 00:01:53.249
think about where you're at

00:01:53.249 --> 00:01:55.543
and think about you not
executing this idea.

00:01:55.543 --> 00:01:57.891
Think about you having
not taken the action

00:01:57.891 --> 00:01:58.856
that you want to take.

00:01:58.856 --> 00:02:00.670
And what that feels like

00:02:00.670 --> 00:02:03.191
to have how many years and years and years

00:02:03.191 --> 00:02:05.619
and years and years and
years and years and years

00:02:05.619 --> 00:02:07.797
of regret not having done the thing

00:02:07.797 --> 00:02:09.757
that you're supposed to
do and is it worth it?

00:02:09.757 --> 00:02:10.883
Whenever I'm afraid,

00:02:10.883 --> 00:02:12.197
whenever I get a no,

00:02:12.197 --> 00:02:14.308
whenever I feel down,

00:02:14.308 --> 00:02:15.902
that's what I try to do.

00:02:15.902 --> 00:02:18.286
If I continue to live thinking like this

00:02:18.286 --> 00:02:19.708
imagine what I'm going to be

00:02:19.708 --> 00:02:22.605
when I'm 150 lookin' back on my life

00:02:22.605 --> 00:02:25.415
wishing that I had taken one more shot.

00:02:25.415 --> 00:02:28.588
Wishing I'd done a little
little little tiny bit more.

00:02:28.588 --> 00:02:31.386
So expect no's, embrace the no's,

00:02:31.386 --> 00:02:33.412
don't be defeated by the no's.

00:02:33.412 --> 00:02:35.265
Get excited by a no.

00:02:35.265 --> 00:02:37.811
Cuz after the no, if you do it again,

00:02:37.811 --> 00:02:39.771
and you do it again, and you do it again,

00:02:39.771 --> 00:02:41.742
eventually you're going to get the yes

00:02:41.742 --> 00:02:43.038
that you deserve.

00:02:43.038 --> 00:02:44.704
So the question today is I'm curious,

00:02:44.704 --> 00:02:46.654
what is the most resourceful thing

00:02:46.654 --> 00:02:48.895
you've ever had to do in your business?

00:02:48.895 --> 00:02:50.234
Leave it in the comments below,

00:02:50.234 --> 00:02:51.733
I'm curious to find out.

00:02:51.733 --> 00:02:53.935
Also want to give a quick
shout out to Gregory Gomes,

00:02:53.935 --> 00:02:56.216
Gregory thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book

00:02:56.216 --> 00:02:58.152
Your One Word, really
means a lot to me man,

00:02:58.152 --> 00:02:59.708
and I hope you're enjoying the read.

00:02:59.708 --> 00:03:01.259
Thank you guys so much for watching,

00:03:01.259 --> 00:03:04.646
I believe in you, I hope you
continue to believe in yourself

00:03:04.646 --> 00:03:06.506
and whatever your one word is,

00:03:06.506 --> 00:03:08.958
much love and I'll see
ya again tomorrow morning

00:03:08.958 --> 00:03:11.588
for another shot of Entspresso.

00:03:11.588 --> 00:03:14.614
♫ I wake up every morning

00:03:14.614 --> 00:03:18.031
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:03:21.303 --> 00:03:23.585
- Well I've launched in the last 16 years

00:03:23.585 --> 00:03:25.718
400 new products,

00:03:25.718 --> 00:03:28.104
and I have 115 patents.

00:03:28.104 --> 00:03:29.840
- People going through this
now have a lot of options,

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:31.953
you have fundraising
sites like Kickstarter,

00:03:31.953 --> 00:03:34.536
you have little online
marketplaces like Etsy.

00:03:34.536 --> 00:03:36.175
Do you recommend that people use these

00:03:36.175 --> 00:03:37.853
to sort of test out their products?

00:03:37.853 --> 00:03:41.533
- I think a lot of people
don't trust their gut enough.

00:03:41.533 --> 00:03:44.179
I think a lot of people want
somebody to hold their hand

00:03:44.179 --> 00:03:45.457
through the process.

00:03:45.457 --> 00:03:47.741
And really that's not the best way.

00:03:47.741 --> 00:03:49.457
There's no special formula that's right

00:03:49.457 --> 00:03:50.882
for every single person.

00:03:50.882 --> 00:03:53.501
You have to decide do
you like Kickstarter,

00:03:53.501 --> 00:03:55.020
do you feel that's right for you?

00:03:55.020 --> 00:03:56.703
Or you know, people have other ways

00:03:56.703 --> 00:03:57.953
in which to do things.

00:03:57.953 --> 00:04:00.335
So I think it's know your options.

00:04:00.335 --> 00:04:02.112
- It's true that I'm a woman in business,

00:04:02.112 --> 00:04:03.787
so are you and it's great

00:04:03.787 --> 00:04:05.938
because they are different personalities,

00:04:05.938 --> 00:04:09.193
successful, be yourself,
take care of business.

00:04:09.193 --> 00:04:10.202
- Be yourself.

00:04:10.202 --> 00:04:11.410
- Go for it, get out there.

00:04:11.410 --> 00:04:12.243
- Yes.

00:04:12.243 --> 00:04:13.581
- But it can be bumpy along the way.

00:04:13.581 --> 00:04:15.467
Any regrets or mistakes
that you feel you've

00:04:15.467 --> 00:04:17.616
kind of hit through the years?

00:04:17.616 --> 00:04:20.315
- Well you know, I share
certain bumps that I've had

00:04:20.315 --> 00:04:21.277
in the book.

00:04:21.277 --> 00:04:23.256
I think that, you know I
don't like to look back,

00:04:23.256 --> 00:04:24.731
there are no mistakes really,

00:04:24.731 --> 00:04:26.155
everything is a learning lesson,

00:04:26.155 --> 00:04:27.820
everything helps you to do better.

00:04:27.820 --> 00:04:28.653
- [Queen Latifah] Right

00:04:28.653 --> 00:04:30.166
- So I talk about some of
the mistakes that I made

00:04:30.166 --> 00:04:31.433
and it just helps you

00:04:31.433 --> 00:04:34.701
to get further along,
learn from those mistakes

00:04:34.701 --> 00:04:36.589
and get smarter.

00:04:36.589 --> 00:04:38.650
True feeling is this,

00:04:38.650 --> 00:04:40.583
no matter who you are,

00:04:40.583 --> 00:04:43.030
no matter what age you are,

00:04:43.030 --> 00:04:45.752
no matter the time in your life,

00:04:45.752 --> 00:04:47.349
if you have a dream,

00:04:47.349 --> 00:04:48.840
and you have the drive,

00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:51.257
you can make anything happen.

00:04:52.324 --> 00:04:55.034
And if you are ever feeling down

00:04:55.034 --> 00:04:57.275
or feeling like you
can't get over that hump,

00:04:57.275 --> 00:04:59.721
or you just have a bad day,

00:04:59.721 --> 00:05:04.524
I play this song, and you
remember this song okay?

00:05:04.524 --> 00:05:05.570
Here it goes.

00:05:05.570 --> 00:05:09.538
♫ This girl is on fire

00:05:09.538 --> 00:05:11.445
(audience applause)

